import pathlib,json,numpy as np,datetime
P=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.load(open(P/'results.json'));d=json.load(open(P/'dataset.json'));f=json.load(open(P/'frozen-before-evaluation.json'));rt=json.load(open(P/'runtime.json'))
lines=['# Real-GPU ASR fingerprinting PoC', '', 'Private research run on Smart NV, 2026-10-25. No product changes, external publishing, paid APIs, model services or diarization.', '', '## Result', '',f"Both selected real models completed timestamped English transcription on the RTX 3090. The fixed 24-value internal summary classified **{int(s['internal']['accuracy']*36)}/36 held-out model/clip pairs** correctly on their first runs; errors across all three instrumented held-out repeats were **{s['all_heldout_instrumented_errors']}/{s['all_heldout_instrumented_n']}**. The output-only timing/rate baseline classified **{int(round(s['output_baseline']['accuracy']*36))}/36** correctly. This supports empirical discrimination between these two exact configurations on this host. It does not authenticate execution or establish resistance to forgery, replay, same-family substitution, or a dishonest measurement collector.", '', '## Data and protocol', '',f"Public LibriSpeech test-clean (CC BY 4.0; Vassil Panayotov et al., LibriVox-derived speech): 30 distinct English utterances, 10 speakers, {sum(r['duration'] for r in d['clips']):.3f} seconds total, {min(r['duration'] for r in d['clips']):.2f}–{max(r['duration'] for r in d['clips']):.2f} seconds each. Exactly the same once-written 16 kHz mono PCM16 WAV paths were passed to both models. Reference text and audio/member/archive SHA256 are in dataset.json. Selection used only duration and sorted source IDs, before inference.", '', 'The split is 12 calibration clips from four speakers and 18 evaluation clips from six different speakers, three utterances per speaker. This deviates from the suggested 10/20 to preserve equal three-clip speaker groups. No speaker or recording chapter crosses the split. Repeats stay in their original split. This is a small, clean read-speech sample, not a broad ASR benchmark.', '',f"The feature/decision method was recorded in config.json before inference. The numerical calibration fit was saved at **{f['frozen_at']}**, before held-out collection. No features, thresholds or classifier were tuned from held-out results. Nearest-centroid classification uses calibration-only class means and pooled within-class feature standard deviations (floor 1e-6); every job receives one of the two class labels, with no unknown-model rejection rule. analyze.py checks the recomputed fit against the saved pre-evaluation fit.", '', '## Real inference and measurements', '', 'Measured parameter counts: Parakeet 627,008,134; Whisper medium.en 762,320,896. Parakeet Hugging Face revision: `541d1f99c6b0c3cd0b11a95167540bb8edefd82b`, .nemo SHA256 `3cbdc85877e668ca7b82d0d56770eb1fac76691f55d6b97545e8d61ca588d10d`. Whisper checkpoint SHA256 `d7440d1dc186f76616474e0ff0b3b6b879abc9d1a4926b7adfa41db2d497ab4f`. Both observed layers 6, 12, 23; both have 1024-wide hidden states here, but learned bases and time resolutions differ.', '', 'Parakeet is nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3 loaded directly using NeMo ASRModel.restore_from on its pinned .nemo checkpoint, eval/CUDA, float32, greedy_batch, native timestamps, batch size one, no CUDA graph decoder. Whisper is OpenAI medium.en loaded through the official inspectable PyTorch package, eval/CUDA, official fp16=True inference, English transcription, word_timestamps=True, temperature=0 without stochastic fallback, no beam/best_of, no previous-text conditioning. All other library defaults are pinned by package/config/source hashes. Models have different decoding and alignment internals. No speaker/VAD/diarization model runs. Seeds are 42, CPU threads four, TF32 and cuDNN benchmarking disabled. Deterministic algorithms were not globally enforced; repeatability is measured rather than guaranteed.', '', 'Three normal PyTorch forward hooks observe relative encoder layers floor(N/4), floor(N/2), and N−1 during complete transcription. Only the first invocation is summarized. Per layer: mean, population standard deviation, standardized third/fourth moments, channel-mean variation/global std, frame-mean variation/global std, adjacent-frame RMS difference/RMS, and adjacent-frame cosine. Statistics use all valid hidden values; only tiny 2×8 activation excerpts are saved as diagnostics. Hooks do not observe the decoder or prove the rest of the pipeline ran.', '', 'NeMo layer pad_mask identifies valid frames; Whisper pooling retains ceil(audio_seconds×50) frames from its fixed 30-second encoder window. Whisper self-attention still sees its padded context. Time resolutions, learned bases, normalizations and precision differ. We compare distributions through a calibration-derived statistical classifier, not elementwise raw state coordinates. Neither tensor shape, input padding, model ID, filenames, byte length, runtime nor timestamp formatting is a classifier input. Ground truth accompanies the feature files as metadata and is not included in the 96-byte numerical payload.', '', 'Calibration-only squared centroid-gap contributions are stored in calibration-contributions.json. The layer-6 activation standard deviation accounts for 70.4% of the standardized squared centroid gap, and layer-12 standard deviation adds 16.5%. Thus much of the separation is a simple activation-scale signature; this is not evidence of a sophisticated content-bound fingerprint. These contributions describe which activation statistics differ, without selecting or refitting features. This classifier learns activation scales/moments and temporal behavior characteristic of the complete model/configuration, potentially including precision and normalization effects. It does not isolate architecture causally and does not show that the summary binds to a particular audio job.', '', 'There are 240 saved complete timed transcriptions: 60 uninstrumented and 180 instrumented. Every model/clip has one instrumented round-0 run and two instrumented round-1 runs after a fresh process/model load. A separate unmeasured full-ASR warm-up precedes each of six invocations. Round-0 baseline/instrumented order alternates across clips. Timers surround the full transcription API, including file decode/preprocessing/timestamp generation, with CUDA synchronization before and after. Downloads/model load and output file writing are excluded. Baselines remove the measurement hooks entirely; active-hook costs include GPU reductions, transfer and CPU synchronization.', '', '## Held-out discrimination and repeatability', '', '| Actual model | Predicted Parakeet | Predicted Whisper |', '|---|---:|---:|']
for m,row in zip(['Parakeet','Whisper'],s['internal']['confusion']):lines.append(f'| {m} | {row[0]} | {row[1]} |')
lines+=['',f"Held-out matched-audio cross-model RMS standardized feature distance: median **{s['cross_heldout']['median']:.6g}**, range **{s['cross_heldout']['min']:.6g}–{s['cross_heldout']['max']:.6g}**. Same-model repeat distance across all clips: median **{s['repeat_all']['median']:.6g}**, maximum **{s['repeat_all']['max']:.6g}**. Reload-pair maximum **{s['repeat_reload']['max']:.6g}** ({s['repeat_reload']['n']} pairs). Repeat pairs are correlated, not independent observations.", '', '| Model | Same-model repeat max | Reload repeat max | Different held-out audio median distance |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for m,x in s['per_model_distances'].items():lines.append(f"| {m} | {x['repeat']['max']:.6g} | {x['reload_repeat']['max']:.6g} | {x['different_audio']['median']:.6g} |")
lines+=['',f"The two models produced identical normalized word sequences for **{s['identical_transcript_clips']}/30** clips, including **{s['identical_transcript_heldout']}/18** held-out clips. Thus classification success includes matched outputs with no normalized transcript-text difference. The output-only baseline uses words/audio-second, mean/std word duration and mean nonnegative interword gap, with the same calibration procedure. It excludes spelling/case/punctuation features, and is only one modest baseline, not a claim that output-only methods cannot distinguish these models.", '',f"Reference-text sanity check after lowercase/alphanumeric token normalization: Parakeet WER **{100*s['quality']['parakeet']['normalized_word_error_rate']:.2f}%**, Whisper **{100*s['quality']['whisper']['normalized_word_error_rate']:.2f}%**. This small selected sample and simple normalization do not support comparative quality claims. Native word boundaries and punctuation differ legitimately; neither is evidence of substitution.", '', '## Collection cost', '', '| Model | Baseline median / mean seconds | Instrumented median / mean seconds | Mean paired change (95% bootstrap CI), ms | Median paired change | Peak allocated / reserved GiB |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for m,t in s['timing'].items():
 ci=t['mean_delta_bootstrap95'];lines.append(f"| {m} | {t['baseline_seconds']['median']:.4f} / {t['baseline_seconds']['mean']:.4f} | {t['instrumented_seconds']['median']:.4f} / {t['instrumented_seconds']['mean']:.4f} | {1000*t['paired_delta_seconds']['mean']:.2f} ({1000*ci[0]:.2f}, {1000*ci[1]:.2f}) | {t['percent']['median']:.2f}% | {t['peak_allocated_GiB']:.3f} / {t['peak_reserved_GiB']:.3f} |")
lines+=['', 'Each timing estimate uses 30 paired clip observations per model. Bootstrap resamples those pairs 5,000 times with seed 42; it does not model correlated speaker/desktop/clock effects. There is one timed baseline per clip, not a fully repeated timing study. Clock warm-up, input length, decoder variability and concurrent desktop use can obscure or reverse small timing differences. Negative overhead samples are noise, not evidence that recording accelerates inference. GPU memory values are PyTorch peaks, excluding other applications and some driver/context allocations; nvidia-smi snapshots supplement them.', '',f"The numeric fingerprint is exactly **96 bytes/job** (24 little-endian float32 values in .f32 sidecars). JSON fingerprints/metadata are larger. Complete raw-text/timestamp JSON job files have median size **{s['json_job_bytes']['median']:.0f} bytes**; measured serialization plus output write median **{1000*s['recording_seconds']['median']:.3f} ms**, max **{1000*s['recording_seconds']['max']:.3f} ms**, recorded separately in recording-times.jsonl. These writes do not fsync. Storage measurements include the full transcript/raw timestamp output, not just fingerprints.", '', 'Process setup/load costs, including imports, restoration and identity hashing where applicable (separate from steady state):', '']
for q in sorted(P.glob('identity-*.json')):
 v=json.load(open(q));lines.append(f"- {q.name}: {v['load_seconds']:.2f} seconds.")
lines+=['', '## Provenance, failures and limits', '',f"Host: smart-nv, normal smart account, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 (24 GiB). Runtime: {rt['packages']}, CUDA {rt['cuda']}. Exact package lock, source hashes, checkpoint SHA256, pinned Hugging Face revision, saved NeMo config, module observation records and GPU process snapshots are included. Whisper checkpoint SHA256 matches its official model URL. The observed dependency freeze retains unused CUDA-13 packages from the failed initial install; requirements.clean.lock is a pruned, constrained fresh-install closure, not an independently rerun environment. All experiment artifacts live under this private research directory; no product repository was changed and nothing was committed, pushed or published.", '', 'The first setup resolved PyTorch 2.14.1, which broke NeMo/Lhotse sampling with `TypeError: object.__init__() takes exactly one argument (the instance to initialize)`. That attempt loaded the model but did not perform successful ASR. The private environment was corrected to torch/torchaudio 2.9.1 and torchvision 0.24.1; successful results use only that stack. smoke-parakeet.log and torch-pin.log preserve the diagnosis. Triton compiled ordinary Whisper alignment kernels during warm-up; compiler warnings are retained. No drivers/system CUDA, production services or model containers were changed. Existing desktop jobs were left running.', '', 'Main limits: two model configurations, one GPU/precision/runtime setup, ten read-speech speakers and only six independent held-out speaker groups. 36 correct first-run decisions do not imply a universal zero error rate; repeated runs are not new audio samples. The classifier always chooses between two known models. There is no unknown-family rejection, fine-grained checkpoint study, cross-hardware study, adversarial integrity claim or defended collector. An attacker could replay or fabricate these compact summaries. Constant architecture-specific scales may be enough for much of the discrimination, and different precision, normalization, quantization or hook placement may change it.', '', '## Recommendation', '', 'Treat this as a reproducible measurement result for these exact candidates, not a protocol mechanism. The small fixed summary is useful for honest-worker diagnostics and experiment comparisons. A separate study would be needed for same-family substitutions, robustness across precision/hardware, audio-job binding and forged fingerprints before considering any verifier design. Do not integrate or assign security/economic weight based on this run.', '', 'Inspect `results.json`, `distances.json`, `runs.csv`, `runs/*.json`, `frozen-before-evaluation.json`, `verification.json` and `separation.png`. Exact commands and dataset/model source links are in README.md. No GPU experiment process should remain after completion; see host-after.txt and completion.json for final cleanup evidence.']
(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
